# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Corsa
# Vauxhall Nova: the UK-market Corsa A, a 3/5-door supermini hatchback.
# UK launch April 1983; production ended March 1993. Nearly 500,000 were sold
# in Britain, with a best year of over 70,000 (7th best-selling car, 1989).
#
# Colours: Flame Red, Estate Blue, Polar White, Black. The DVSA colour table
# starts at 1994 registrations; its 1994-96 survivor shares (blue 23-25%,
# red 19-23%, white 7-10%, black 8-10%) are used as the measured base, with
# white and red weighted up because they were stronger on 1980s registrations.
# Paint names are Vauxhall marketing names for the approximate shades; the
# render values are approximations, not paint codes.
#
# Intro/retire dates describe when that colour would be seen regularly on UK
# roads, not the production dates. Weights total 46 against the Escort Mk3's
# 100, matching the Nova's roughly half-Escort UK volume.

